  "reason": "Evidence: PCA n2000 single-profile RNA (config_001, acc=0.485) is the best configuration so far, clearly outperforming scGPT single-profile (0.411) and image-only ResNet50 (0.208). The image modality appears weak, so the primary direction for improvement is likely within the RNA pipeline. Question: Does multiprofile aggregation (avgpool) improve upon the best single-profile RNA encoder? config_002 is a minimal single-variable extension of config_001—same encoder (PCA n2000), same modality (RNA only), but adding multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool). This cleanly isolates the effect of multiprofile without confounding changes to encoder or fusion. Why this is the best next step: With 6 experiments remaining, establishing whether multiprofile helps the strongest RNA encoder before investing in multimodal fusion or more complex aggregators (transformer) is the most information-efficient move. If avgpool helps, we can then test transformer; if not, we can pivot to scVI or multimodal with confidence that the single-profile ceiling is well-characterized."
